1. Identity Basics (Core Concept)
👉 Everything starts here:

Identity = Who the user/system is
Examples:
Employee login (john@company.com)
Application identity (service principal)


IdP vs SP (Most IMPORTANT)

IdP (Identity Provider) Authenticates user
SP (Service Provider)   Application user accesses


Real Azure Example

Azure Entra ID = IdP
Your internal app / Salesforce = SP

👉 Flow:
User opens app
App redirects to Entra ID
User logs in
Entra sends token → app trusts it

SSO (Single Sign-On)
🔹 Beginner Understanding
One login → access multiple apps


✅ Real Example
Employee logs into:
Outlook
Teams
ServiceNow

👉 Only logs in once using Entra ID

Federation
🔹 Simple Idea
👉 Trust between identity systems

✅ Real Example
Your company uses Entra ID
Vendor uses Okta

👉 You configure federation:
Your Entra trusts their Okta
Now external users log into YOUR apps


